  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Ministry of Statistics &amp; Programme Implementation, National Statistical Office. Household Consumption Expenditure Survey, 2022-23 and 2023-24 rounds, retrieved via the eSankhyiki API, vintage <b id="prov-vintage" set:html={TX["prov-vintage"]}></b>.</p>
        <p>Two disclosures carry through every chart. First, the headline convention is "without imputation"; the with-imputation variants are shown and named where used. Cereal quantities are published in that convention only. Second, only these two rounds exist in the API: the 2011-12 and earlier NSS consumption rounds use a different method, are not served, and are never spliced or compared here.</p>
        <p>All nine indicator families of the HCES release are baked into this guide's data, every one by state and for both conventions where the survey publishes both. The broad-category table in rupees feeds the state spending tables; its shares twin feeds the food-share map.</p>
        <p><b>A misprint at source.</b> In the rupee table for 2022-23, rural, without imputation, the rows printed under Goa, Gujarat, Haryana, Himachal Pradesh, Jharkhand and Karnataka are those of Andhra Pradesh, Arunachal Pradesh, Assam, Bihar, Chhattisgarh and Delhi: each block adds up to the other state's MPCE to the rupee. Those six cells are left out; the same cells of the share table are consistent and are kept. The 2023-24 round is unaffected.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>Survey estimates are final on release. Each round is a cross-section; the two rounds are comparable by design but are never averaged or chained. All figures are sample estimates and carry sampling error the published tables do not quantify.</p>
        <p>Where something is not measured, incomes, prices, the far top of the distribution, this guide says "we do not know" rather than inventing a number.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Consumption, version 1.2 (October 2026), on the 2023-24 round. v1.1 extended the first release with the social-group, household-type, cereal-quantity, cereal-value and state food-share families; v1.2 adds every indicator by state, the rupee spending tables, the with-imputation figures by state and inequality by state. Next scheduled revision: on release of the next HCES round.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fine">
      <span>Measure of India, HCES</span>
      <span>Vintage <span id="prov-vintage2" set:html={TX["prov-vintage2"]}></span>, never spliced with 2011-12</span>
      <span>Set in Newsreader and Libre Franklin</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

